# AION × Superpowers bridge (product repo)

This product repo uses [obra/superpowers](https://github.com/obra/superpowers) as **session process**, layered under AION governance from the [AION Software Factory](https://github.com/AION-Sys/aion-software-factory).

## Priority (highest first)

1. Explicit human/CEO instruction for this turn
2. Factory `AION_ENGINEERING.md` + active mission + this repo `AGENTS.md`
3. Product `docs/PRD.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, task scope
4. Factory workflows/standards (via factory repo links)
5. Superpowers skills (if the plugin is installed)
6. Default agent behavior

## Before creative or implementation work

1. Confirm MISSION-002 scope and acceptance criteria; do not invent Mission 003 product work.
2. Prefer Superpowers `brainstorming` for new behavior; write outcomes into product docs / architecture notes, not only chat.
3. Prefer `writing-plans` mapped to existing Architect tasks before large code changes.
4. Prefer `test-driven-development` for logic changes; run this repo’s `npm` quality checks.
5. Prefer `verification-before-completion` before any "done / fixed / passing" claim.
6. Prefer `systematic-debugging` before speculative bugfixes.

## Hard stops Superpowers must not override

- CEO approval gates (mission scope, production deploy, release, validation close)
- Secrets in git/logs/prompts
- Mission 002 out-of-scope items (autonomous calling, CRM replacement, workflow builder)
- Opening Mission 003 product work while Mission 002 validation is open
- Expanding beyond the assigned architecture task without human approval

## Role shortcuts (Builder-focused)

| Role | Lean on |
|------|---------|
| Builder | worktrees → executing-plans/TDD → small PR in **this** repo |
| QA | verification-before-completion → evidence vs acceptance criteria |
| Security | systematic-debugging for investigations; no silent secret commits |
| Release | verification smoke; never silent prod ship |

